### Steps to reproduce issue

Build and run `./jump_probe cbg`, then compare with `single` and `multi`.

The program runs two nodes:
- `clock_pub` publishes `/clock` every 20 ms.
- `subject` uses `use_sim_time: true` with three 100 ms timers: ROS (`create_timer`), steady (`create_wall_timer`), and system (`RCL_SYSTEM_TIME`).

The clock runs for 2 s from 1000 s, jumps backward to 900 s for 2 s, then forward to 1004 s for 2 s.

**Variants:**
- `late`: Enables `use_sim_time` after timer creation and executor startup.
- `reset`: Resets the ROS timer immediately after the backward jump.

```cpp
#include <atomic>
#include <chrono>
#include <cstdio>
#include <memory>
#include <string>
#include <thread>

#include <rclcpp/executors/events_cbg_executor/events_cbg_executor.hpp>
#include <rclcpp/experimental/executors/events_executor/events_executor.hpp>
#include <rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp>
#include <rosgraph_msgs/msg/clock.hpp>

using namespace std::chrono_literals;

int main(int argc, char ** argv)
{
  const std::string kind = argc > 1 ? argv[1] : "cbg";
  const std::string mode = argc > 2 ? argv[2] : "-";
  const bool reset_after_jump = mode == "reset";
  const bool late_sim_time = mode == "late";
  rclcpp::init(argc, argv);

  auto clock_node = std::make_shared<rclcpp::Node>("clock_pub");
  auto pub = clock_node->create_publisher<rosgraph_msgs::msg::Clock>("/clock", rclcpp::ClockQoS());

  rclcpp::NodeOptions opts;
  if (!late_sim_time) {
    opts.parameter_overrides({rclcpp::Parameter("use_sim_time", true)});
  }
  auto subject = std::make_shared<rclcpp::Node>("subject", opts);
  std::atomic<int> ros_fires{0}, steady_fires{0}, system_fires{0};
  auto ros_timer = subject->create_timer(100ms, [&] {++ros_fires;});
  auto steady_timer = subject->create_wall_timer(100ms, [&] {++steady_fires;});
  auto system_clock = std::make_shared<rclcpp::Clock>(RCL_SYSTEM_TIME);
  auto system_timer = rclcpp::create_timer(
    subject, system_clock, rclcpp::Duration{100ms}, [&] {++system_fires;});

  std::shared_ptr<rclcpp::Executor> exec;
  if (kind == "single") {
    exec = std::make_shared<rclcpp::executors::SingleThreadedExecutor>();
  } else if (kind == "multi") {
    exec = std::make_shared<rclcpp::executors::MultiThreadedExecutor>(rclcpp::ExecutorOptions{}, 2);
  } else if (kind == "events") {
    exec = std::make_shared<rclcpp::experimental::executors::EventsExecutor>();
  } else {
    exec = std::make_shared<rclcpp::executors::EventsCBGExecutor>(rclcpp::ExecutorOptions{}, 2);
  }
  exec->add_node(subject);
  std::thread spinner{[&] {exec->spin();}};

  if (late_sim_time) {
    std::this_thread::sleep_for(200ms);
    subject->set_parameter(rclcpp::Parameter("use_sim_time", true));
  }

  rosgraph_msgs::msg::Clock msg;
  const auto play = [&](std::int64_t start_ns, const char * phase) {
      const int r0 = ros_fires, s0 = steady_fires, y0 = system_fires;
      for (int i = 0; i < 100; ++i) {  // 2 s of sim time at real rate, in 20 ms steps
        msg.clock = rclcpp::Time{start_ns + i * 20'000'000LL};
        pub->publish(msg);
        std::this_thread::sleep_for(20ms);
      }
      std::printf(
        "%-6s %-5s %-28s ros=%2d steady=%2d system=%2d\n", kind.c_str(), mode.c_str(),
        phase, ros_fires - r0, steady_fires - s0, system_fires - y0);
    };
  play(1000'000'000'000LL, "before jump (1000 s)");
  if (reset_after_jump) {
    msg.clock = rclcpp::Time{900'000'000'000LL};
    pub->publish(msg);
    std::this_thread::sleep_for(50ms);
    ros_timer->reset();
  }
  play(900'000'000'000LL, "after backward jump (900 s)");
  play(1004'000'000'000LL, "after forward jump (1004 s)");

  exec->cancel();
  spinner.join();
  rclcpp::shutdown();
  return 0;
}
```

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)
project(jump_probe CXX)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
find_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)
find_package(rosgraph_msgs REQUIRED)
add_executable(jump_probe jump_probe.cpp)
target_link_libraries(jump_probe rclcpp::rclcpp ${rosgraph_msgs_TARGETS})
```

### Expected behavior

The timer on the ROS clock keeps firing through the backward jump, as it does on `SingleThreadedExecutor` and `MultiThreadedExecutor`, and it starts firing once `use_sim_time` is enabled late.

### Actual behavior

Timer callbacks per 2 s phase (20 expected), rolling at bca9dffc:

| Executor | mode | before jump (1000 s) | after backward jump (900 s) | after forward jump (1004 s) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `SingleThreadedExecutor` | - | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 | ros=19 steady=20 system=20 | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 |
| `MultiThreadedExecutor` | - | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 | ros=19 steady=20 system=20 | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 |
| `EventsCBGExecutor` | - | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 | **ros=0** steady=20 system=20 | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 |
| `EventsCBGExecutor` | late | **ros=0** steady=20 system=20 | **ros=0** steady=20 system=20 | **ros=0** steady=20 system=20 |
| `EventsCBGExecutor` | reset | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 | ros=19 steady=20 system=20 | ros=20 steady=21 system=21 |
| `EventsExecutor` (experimental) | - | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 | ros=19 steady=20 system=20 | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 |
| `EventsExecutor` (experimental) | late | ros=19 steady=20 system=20 | ros=19 steady=20 system=20 | ros=20 steady=20 system=20 |

With `EventsCBGExecutor` the ROS clock timer resumes only once simulated time passes the deadline it had before the jump, so with `ros2 bag play --loop --clock` it fires once per loop at best. In the `late` case the timer keeps a deadline in system time (about 1.76e9 s) and never fires for any realistic simulated time. Steady and system clock timers are unaffected on every executor, and forward jumps are fine.

### Additional information

**Root cause:** `rcl` rebases timer deadlines on backward clock jumps and ROS time activation/deactivation without invoking the on-reset callback (intentional per ros2/rcl#995). `EventsCBGExecutor` caches these deadlines in `TimerQueue::running_timers`, which is only updated on timer creation, callback completion, or reset.

After a clock jump, `timer_thread()` keeps sleeping against the stale deadline even though `ClockWaiter` wakes it on every clock sample. The timer never fires because its updated deadline isn't reflected in the queue.

Calling `timer->reset()` re-keys the timer and restores execution. Wait-set executors and the experimental `EventsExecutor` are unaffected because they re-query `rcl` deadlines.

**Workaround:** Reset sim-time timers in a post-jump callback configured with a negative `min_backward` threshold. For late ROS time activation, create timers after enabling `use_sim_time`.
